<BRL/><BRL/><BRL/><BRL/><BRL/><BRL/><BRL/><BRL/><BRL/><BRL/><BRL/><BRL/><BRL/><BRL/><BRL/><BRL/><BRL/></TAB><BRK/></TXT>
<BRK/>
<TXT>Where 0 percent payment is indicated, remove the entire lot and replace at no additional cost to the Government.  Where either of the two cores 
from a sublot show a thickness deficiency of<MET> 19 mm</MET><ENG> 0.75 inch</ENG> or greater, [<MET>13 mm</MET><ENG>0.50 inch</ENG> for pavements<MET> 200 mm</MET><ENG> 8 inches</ENG> or less in thickness] drill 
two more cores in the sublot and compute the average thickness of the four cores.  If this average shows a thickness deficiency of<MET> 19 mm</MET><ENG> 0.75 inch</ENG>
 or more [<MET>13 mm</MET><ENG>0.50 inch</ENG> for pavements<MET> 200 mm</MET><ENG> 8 inches</ENG> or less in thickness] remove the entire sublot.</TXT><BRK/>
<BRK/></SPT>
